fund-csharp/12-async-await-and-tasks/01-.explanation:
Materialise the tasks with `ToList()` so every fetch starts immediately, then await them together; `Task.WhenAll` returns results in the order of the tasks you passed:

```csharp
var tasks = symbols.Select(s => fetch(s, ct)).ToList();
var prices = await Task.WhenAll(tasks);
return symbols.Select((s, i) => new Quote(s, prices[i])).ToList();
```

A `foreach` with `await fetch(...)` inside passes the order and token tests but fails the concurrency test (peak 1). Forgetting `ToList()` and enumerating the deferred `Select` twice would start every fetch twice.

